Rather than touching 6 call sites, the cleanest hook: call `renderSuggestions()` at the end of `renderGroupOrders()` — but renderGroupOrders returns early when no orders (`return` after empty message). I'll restructure: rename? Minimal edit: in renderGroupOrders, replace the early `return` with rendering suggestions first... Actually simplest: at the top of renderGroupOrders add `renderSuggestions();` and remove the early return problem — the early return happens after `elements.groupOrders.textContent = ''` + empty message + return. If renderSuggestions() is called first, suggestions still render. 

So:
```js
function renderGroupOrders() {
  if (!session) return;
  renderSuggestions();
  ...
}
```
One-line hook covering all call sites. 

renderSuggestions:
```js
function renderSuggestions() {
  if (!elements.suggestionsCard) return;
  const suggestions = (session && session.suggestions) || [];
  elements.suggestionsCard.hidden = !suggestions.length;
  elements.suggestionsList.textContent = '';
  suggestions.forEach((suggestion) => {
    card: person, drink h3, detail, qty
    actions (only when session.accepting_orders):
      Confirm (primary compact) → confirmSuggestion(suggestion, {}, button)
      Change → changeSuggestion(suggestion)
      Not me (text-button) → dismissSuggestion(suggestion, button)
  });
}
```

confirmSuggestion(suggestion, payload, button):
```js
async function confirmSuggestion(suggestion, payload, button) {
  if (button) button.disabled = true;
  setFormStatus(`Confirming ${suggestion.drink} for ${suggestion.person}…`, 'busy');
  try {
    const data = await request(`${apiBase}/suggestions/${encodeURIComponent(suggestion.id)}/confirm`, {
      method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify(payload),
    });
    setSession(data.session);
    rememberOrder(data.order.id, data.order_token);
    writeStorage(participantNameKey, data.order.person);  // hmm — confirming someone else's name shouldn't overwrite my stored name. Only update stored name if it matches current input? Skip this. Actually submitOrder writes person input to storage. For confirm-as-is, don't touch name storage. For change-flow, payload person comes from input; submitOrder-equivalent handles. To keep simple: don't write name storage in confirmSuggestion; the change path goes through submitOrder which does.
    confirmingSuggestionId = null;
    resetEditor({keepStatus: true});
    setFormStatus(`${data.order.drink} confirmed for ${data.order.person}.`, 'ok');
    renderRoom(); renderGroupOrders(); refreshLeaderboard();
  } catch (error) {
    setFormStatus(error.message, 'err');
    if (button) button.disabled = false;
  }
}
```
